{"event":"result","result":{"conversation_id":"dcfafc8d-78b6-476f-9240-5ee032d8b933","status":"SUCCESS","response":"The issues causing the failure of the Intervals.icu connection and the 1-hour disconnect have been identified and resolved, and the causes documented in [ANSWER.md](file:///tmp/h-wsotAj/ANSWER.md).\n\n### Summary of Root Causes and Fixes\n\n1. **Connect Button 401 Unauthorized**:\n   - **Cause**: The Connect button in [static/app.js](file:///tmp/h-wsotAj/static/app.js) was a standard `\u003ca\u003e` link to `/api/intervals/auth/init`. Full-page browser navigation does not send the client auth token stored in `localStorage` (`Authorization: Bearer`), causing the backend to return 401.\n   - **Fix**: Updated `/api/intervals/auth/init` in [server.py](file:///tmp/h-wsotAj/server.py) to support authenticated `POST` requests returning `{ \"authorize_url\": ... }`, and updated [static/app.js](file:///tmp/h-wsotAj/static/app.js) to call it using the authenticated `api()` fetch wrapper before redirecting via `window.location.assign()`.\n\n2. **HTTP 400 Bad Request on Intervals.icu Consent Screen (\"Duplicate scope\")**:\n   - **Cause**: [config.py](file:///tmp/h-wsotAj/config.py) configured `SCOPES` requesting both `:READ` and `:WRITE` for the same area (`ACTIVITY:READ,ACTIVITY:WRITE,CALENDAR:READ,CALENDAR:WRITE`). Intervals.icu treats `:WRITE` as implying `:READ` and rejects duplicate area mentions with an error.\n   - **Fix**: Cleaned the scope string in [config.py](file:///tmp/h-wsotAj/config.py) to `\"ACTIVITY:WRITE,WELLNESS:READ,CALENDAR:WRITE\"`.\n\n3. **Athlete Told to Reconnect After an Hour (\"expired, reconnect\")**:\n   - **Cause**: Intervals.icu tokens do not expire or return `refresh_token`s. The backend imposed a default 1-hour TTL (`DEFAULT_TOKEN_TTL = 3600`) and a background thread `refresh_tokens()`, which marked the token as expired when no refresh token was found after 1 hour.\n   - **Fix**: Removed the artificial expiration timer and background refresher in [server.py](file:///tmp/h-wsotAj/server.py). Tokens are retained indefinitely until revoked (lazy revocation handling when receiving 401 responses on API calls).\n\n4. **Token Exchange Parameters**:\n   - **Cause**: `exchange_code()` sent standard OAuth parameters (`grant_type`, `redirect_uri`) not used by Intervals.icu's token endpoint.\n   - **Fix**: Adjusted the token exchange call to send only `client_id`, `client_secret`, and `code`.\n","duration_seconds":102.950355,"num_turns":1,"usage":{"input_tokens":138084,"output_tokens":4257,"thinking_tokens":0,"cache_read_tokens":561881,"total_tokens":142341}}}
